d is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christian Ian Brown | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $308K ranks in the bottom quartile among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $834 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Centuri Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $2.2B market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 8% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $8M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 600% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":6.0036703495604105},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $29.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-29697590.76},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Utilities peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Growing faster than most Utilities peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Centuri (NYSE:CTRI) Director Acquires $99,990.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/centuri-nysectri-director-acquires-99990-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586148.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Insider Selling: Centuri (NYSE:CTRI) Major Shareholder Sells $5,682,250.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnia