e models disagree (dispersion 17%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Utilities peers: P/E 38.3 vs 20.3 (sector median).","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -0.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 7 covering analysts target $27.86 on average, 28% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 6% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have been steady (CV 0.02).","It runs a 8% gross margin and burns cash (FCF margin -0%).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 3.49x.","ROE of 3% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 3.0x net debt to EBITDA ($126.6M of cash against $737.6M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, and interest cover is thin at 1.4x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 13.1% over 3 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 6.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.05 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 14% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 102%.","Capex runs only 0.8x depreciation (2.9% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 3 purchases and 4 sales over the past year, net $29.7M sold."],"people":["With about 9,687 employees, each generates about $308K of revenue, 0.3x the Utilities median.","CEO pay is $2.6M (8x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":23,"head":"Avoid: priced 600% above its fair value of $3.12.","pros":["Revenue grew 13.1%/yr over 3y","7 analysts' mean t